# Pathfinder

Read `docs/PLAN.md` before implementing. Do the next unchecked step only, then mark that step done in the same change.

- TypeScript, React, and Node. One Render web service from the root Dockerfile. Listen on `0.0.0.0` and `process.env.PORT`. `GET /health` stays available.
- One secret: `MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN` in the repo-root `.env` (gitignored). The server reads it at runtime. The browser fetches the public token from the server. Do not add a second token variable, and do not log the token.
- No accounts. Stops and the round-trip toggle persist in `localStorage`.
- Mapbox Optimization API, profile `mapbox/driving`, 2–12 stops. Round trip is a toolbar toggle (`roundtrip=true`, or `roundtrip=false` with `source=any` and `destination=any`).
- On load, restore the saved map center and zoom. If none was saved and stops exist, frame the stops. If there is no saved view and no stops, ask for the browser location. If that is denied or unavailable, center the map on Minsk (longitude 27.559, latitude 53.9006).
- Desktop first. The map fills the page. The upper-left toolbar carries the logo and name and keeps its width and rounded corners, so a later mobile layout can stack the toolbar and the map.
